      "content": "here are the docs:\n\n[Client Specs - Project Helios]:\nA multi-junction thin-film solar cell utilizing a proprietary perovskite-silicon tandem structure. The key innovation is the application of a specific nano-textured interlayer between the perovskite and the silicon sub-cell to reduce reflective losses and improve charge carrier extraction efficiency via a gradient bandgap approach.\n\n[Prior Art Database]:\n1. Patent US-2021-004567-A1: High-efficiency tandem solar cells using silicon-based substrates.\n2. Patent US-2018-098765-B2: Perovskite-silicon tandem solar cells utilizing a nano-textured interlayer for improved light trapping and interface carrier transport.\n3. Patent US-2015-123456-A1: Standard thin-film photovoltaic architecture with graded bandgap layers.\n\nGo ahead and do the comparison. I need that novelty summary so I can get this in front of the board by tomorrow morning. We can't afford any delays on this one.",
